{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>To sojourn in the land we have come, for there is no pasture for the flocks that your servants have.</b> I am puzzled by this reasoning that they gave him, for in Egypt too there is no pasture, since the famine was severe in the land of Egypt just as in the land of Canaan, or even more so, for upon it was the main force of the decree. Perhaps they said that in the land of Canaan, because of the severity of the famine, the people would eat the grass of the field and leave no sustenance for the animals, but in the land of Egypt there is provision through which the people would live, and some pasture would remain in it. And it is possible that there was a little pasture in the land of Egypt in the marshland, because of the rivers and the pools."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:45:48.035427100Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}